# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-14 — command-lane artifacts and corpora. Additive only; nothing
# above this line was changed.
#
# `deploy.sh` ships `--source .`, which uploads UNTRACKED files too. These
# 23 paths were entering the Cloud Build context for that reason alone, not
# because anything wanted them there. `corpus/` (2.2 M) carries third-party
# newsletter content under a standing no-upload constraint.
#
# Deliberately NOT globbed. `*.md` would drop ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md and
# CHANGELOG.md; `*.txt` would drop requirements.txt, which the build needs.
# Entries below name untracked paths only, so no tracked file leaves the
# upload set. New untracked files under these trees are covered by the
# directory entries; new ones beside a named file are not, and will ship
# until named.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
corpus/
review_packets/
drafts/
command_structure/doctrine/
command_structure/sop/
command_structure/README.md
command_structure/ROADMAP.md
command_structure/VOCABULARY.md
# 2026-08-21 — snapshots/ promoted to a directory entry (was 7 named
# files; 5 newer handoffs shipped into the build context before this —
# the file's own "will ship until named" prediction). Whole tree is
# command-lane artifacts, nothing runtime.
snapshots/
source_docs/ClarityOS_SOS_integrated_ops_map_2026-08-14.mmd
source_docs/returns_2026-08-05_control_language_draft.txt
specs/D1_CT2_REVIEW.md
specs/SPEC_LINE_B_lexicon_v1_2026-08-10_COW1.md
ClarityOS_ClarityEngine_Background_SocialThermodynamics.md
SPEC_READER_GROUNDING_v0.1_DRAFT.md
et1_prod_env_reads_return_2026-07-08_1220EDT_v1.md
et1_public_base_url_reconciliation_return_2026-07-08_1526EDT_v1.md
kimi_endstate_walk_return_2026-08-20_1105EDT_v1.md

